1. **Polymorphic property**: No two infections have the same byte signature (the decryptor is mutated, and the main body is encrypted with a new key every time), so signature-based antivirus will fail to detect all variants.
2. **Consistent functionality**: All variants behave identically, only their code syntax changes.

